    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-12-13 11:44\nmodified: 2025-12-13 21:56\n---\nHere we pass from numbers $dx$ to matrices $dA$.\n\nA standard identity is, when $f$ is scalar. If this were classic Multivariable Calculus then $\\nabla_{A}f$ would be a column vector, but here is a matrix. At the end is like resize the vector wisely. \n$$\ndf= \\mathrm{Tr}((\\nabla_{A}f)^{\\mathsf{\\top}}dA)\n$$",
    "uploadDate": "2025-12-13 11:44",
