    "id": "175",
    "title": "Unit",
    "excerpt": "There exist seven fundamental units.",
    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-11-10 14:41\nmodified: 2025-11-10 15:04\n---\nThere exist seven fundamental units.\n\n\n|Fundamental Units | Unit  |\n| --- | --- |\n|  Time - Defined via Cesium - 133 transition period  |   $\\text{s}$  |\n|  Distance - Defined via light speed  |  $\\text{m}$   |\n| Mass - Defined by the [[Planck constant]] | $\\text{Kg}$  |\n| Temperature - Defined by the [[Boltzmann constant]] | $\\text{K}$ |\n| Ampere - Defined by the charge of the electron | $\\text{A}$ |\n| Mole Defined via **Avogadro Number** | $\\text{mol}$ |\n| Candela Defined by the luminous efficacy of monochromatic radiation ? | $\\text{cd}$ |\n\n\n- The meter defined using the [[Speed Of Light]] [^1]\n- Second define using the Cesium-133\n- Cande\n\n[^1]: [[Fisica Universitaria]] pp. 28\n",
    "uploadDate": "2025-11-10 14:41",
    "readTime": "4 min read",
    "fileName": "Unit.md",
    "featured": false
