    "excerpt": ">A point $x\\in X$ is called interior of a subset $X$ when exist a open interval $(a,b)\\subset X$ such that $x\\in(a,b)$. [^1]",
    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-11-04 09:21\nmodified: 2025-11-04 09:56\n---\n>[!definition]\n>A point $x\\in X$ is called interior of a subset $X$ when exist a open interval $(a,b)\\subset X$ such that $x\\in(a,b)$. [^1]\n\n- To the set of all those points we call $\\text{int}$.\n\n>[!definition]\n>A set is **open** if $\\text{int}(X)=X$.\n\n- This is more important to define the open sets in the reals.\n- There exist a close relation with [[Open Set]].  \n\n[^1]: [[Analisis Real Elon Lages]] pp. 65\n",
