    "id": "236",
    "title": "Linear Algebra   2025 II",
    "excerpt": "|**Linear Algebra**     | **2025-II**    |",
    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-10-30 13:00\nmodified: 2026-01-12 08:46\n---\n|**Linear Algebra**     | **2025-II**    |\n| --- | --- |\n| Professor    | Alejandro Paredes    |\n| Practical Professor | Caro |\n| Place | R1-128-448 J3 248|\n| Schedule | Thursday Friday 4-6 |\n| Code | CF2C1 | \n| Capstone | I only see paper, nothing computational here. My actual project is good enough|\n\n## Week 1 : Inner product\n- [ ] 1.1 [[Inner product]]\n- [ ] 1.2 [[Euclid Vector Space]]\n\n## Week 2: Gram Matrix, Ortogonalization\n- [ ] 2.1 [[Gram matrix]]\n- [ ] 2.2 [[Orthonormal basis]]\n\n## Week 3: Gram Schmidt Procedure\n- [ ] 3.1 [[Gram Schimdt Procedure]]\n- [ ] 3.2 [[Orthogonal complement]]\n\n## Week 4: Adjoint \n- [ ] 4.1 [[Self Adjoint Operators]]\n- [ ] 4.2 [[Adjoint Operator]]\n\n## Week 5: Ortogonal Spectral Theorem\n\n- [ ] 5.1 [[Orthogonal operator]] [[Polar Descomposition]]\n- [ ] 5.2 [[Spectral theorem Real Version]]\n\n## Week 6 : Complex Vector Spaces I (Oct)\n\n- [ ] 6.1 [[Hermitian space]]\n- [ ] 6.2 First definitions?\n\n## Week 7 : Complex Vector Spaces II (Oct 14 -21)\n\n- [ ] 7.1  [[Unitary Operator]] [[Normal Operators]]\n- [ ] 7.2 [[simultaneously diagonalizable]]\n\n## Week 8: Exam Week\n\n1. Question about the [[Hermite polinomials]], prove certain properties and use a linear operator with it.\n2. Recall\n3. Hermitian Operators. Relation between Unitary Operator and [[Unitary Hermitian Exponential]], use certain approximation.\n\n## Week 9 : Dirac Notation (Oct 21- 28)\n\n- [ ] 9.1 [[Expected Value For Operators]], [[Operators are ket bra]], [[Completeness Relation]], [[Bra ket notation for make us the life easier]], [[Adjoint Operator Demystified]]\n\n## Week 10. Application of the Dirac Notation and Tensor product (Nov 3 - 7)\n\n- [x] 10.1 Angular Momentum Demystified [[Angular momentum on QC]]. [[Direct Sum]] [[tensor product]] Eigen States, [[Direct Sum of Linear Maps]] [[Direct Kronecker Product]]\n- [x] 10.2 [[Angular Momentum Addition]] [[Hilber Space Spin 1 and 12]] [[General Theory of Spin]] [[Hilbert Space Spin 1]] [[Hilbert Space Spin 1 2]] [[Angular Operators Spin 1]]\n\n### Guided Practice\n\n**Guided Practice**: Practicing with ket and bras\n\n## Week 11 (Nov 7 - 14) Spin Theory using Dirac Notation\n   \n- [x] 11.1 Spins in greater spaces, physical intuition spin, Hilbert space, a brief introduction to simplectic spaces, spins on magnetic fields.\n- [x] 11.2 Symplectic Spaces 1. First definitions, sympletic basis, [[Symplectic Vector Space]]\n\n- [x] **Home Work:** Prove that $\\mathcal{H}_{\\frac{1}{2}}\\otimes \\mathcal{H}_{\\frac{1}{2}}=\\mathcal{H}_{1}\\oplus \\mathcal{H}_{0}$ [[Home Work 1]]\n### 11. 1 Qualified Practice\n1. Bra Ket Notation\n2. Kronecker Product\n3. Projector Operators, demonstrations of the eigen values, value expectation\n4. Inner product defined with the Kronecker Product\n   \n## Week 12 (Nov 14-21)\n\n- [ ] 12.1 Simplectic Spaces, Lagrangian, MAS via the [[Hamilton Equations]], [[Lagrangian]], [[Generalized Coordinates]].\n- [ ] 12.2 Canonical Form, Tensor, [[Canonical Transform]]. Pseudo Vector [[Canonical Transform Requeriment]] invertibility of transform, the invariance of the hamiltonian. [[Contravariance Vectors]] [[Covariance Vectors]] ideas.\n- [x] **Home Work** Prove if the [[Galilean Transformation]], and the [[Polar Coordinate System]] are [[Canonical Transform]].\n\n### 12. 1 Laboratory Session\n\n The [[Coupled Oscillators]].\n\n## Week 13 (Nov 22- 28)\n\n- [ ] 13.1 [[Vector formal definition]].\n- [ ] 13.2 Scalar Definition, [[Contravariance Vectors]], [[Covariance Vectors]]. [[Tensor formal definition]] [[Index Tensors]]\n- [ ] **Homework**. Prove that the sum of tensors $(r,s)$ is another tensor, [[tensor product]] of tensors  is another tensor.\n\n### 13.1 Guided Practice (Nov 24)\n\n [[Direct Sum]] Intern and extern, angular momentum and spin, casimiro operator, [[Total Angular Momentum Operator]], spherics armonical, phase of space. [[Simplectic Matrix]]\n \n## Week 14 (Dec 02 - Dec 07)\n\n- [ ] 14.1 [[Symmetry Tensors]], [[Contraction of Tensors]].\n- [ ] 14.2 [[Electromagnetic Tensors]]. [[Change index Tensors]].\n\n### 14.1 Qualified Practice (Dec 01)\n\n1. Direct Sum, intern and extern.\n2. [[Angular Momentum Addition]], prove the sum product relation. I do it wrong. It was $\\{ 0,1 \\}$\n3. Simplectic Forms. \n4. Index notation property for [[Orthogonal operator]], what form should take the gram matrix. [[Levi-Civita Symbol]] for the expresion: $\\vec{a}\\times(\\vec{b}\\times \\vec{c})$.\n\n### 14. 2 Laboratory Session: Discomposing any matrix into a triangular and a orthogonal matrix.\n\n**Personal Future Research**.- Tensor Networks for Quantum Computation and Many body quantum states. I mean they are not just useful for Special Relativity. \n\n## Week 16 (Dec 15)\n\n1. Inertia tensor, it will be a tensor $(r,s)$?. Yeah exactly that. And even with it, I wasn't able to do it.\n2. Electromagnetic Tensors. Yeah, exactly that.\n3. Canonical Transform. Easy\n4. [[Expected Value For Operators]]. Easy.",
