    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-10-29 19:46\nmodified: 2026-01-19 07:17\n---\n\n| Real Analisis  | 2025 - II    |\n| --- | --- |\n| Professor Name | Munguia |\n| Practice professor |  Fidel Castro |\n| Schedule|  Thursday and Friday 182-B 1:00 4:00 PM |\n| Code |  CM2A2 |\n\nMusts: Silabo Dosificado Curricalar 3\n\n## Week 1: Natural numbers\n\n- [ ] 1.1 Natural Numbers, Definition of the successor of a number, and fundamental theorem of arithmetics\n- [ ] 1.2 Operations of the natural numbers.\n- [ ] 1.3 The good order principle.\n\n## Week 2: Sets and function\n\n- [ ] 2.1 Finite Sets. \n- [ ] 2.2 Countable sets. Properties\n- [ ] 2.3 Real Numbers. Definition\n\n## Week 3: Real Numbers\n- [ ] 3.1 Completeness theorem\n- [ ] 3.2 The non countless of the real numbers. Supreme Theorem\n- [ ] 3.3 Limit of a sequence, and inequalities\n\n## Week 4: Defining real numbers\n\n- [ ] 4.1 Inferior and superior limit, [[Cauchy Sequences defining the real numbers]]\n- [ ] 4.2  Completeness of R, infinite limits of sequences\n- [ ] 4.3 Sequences.\n\n## Week 5: Sequences\n\n- [ ] 5.1 Sequences dirichlet, [[Absolutely Convergent Series]]\n- [ ] 5.2 [[Cauchy's Criterion For Sequences]] Abel Criterion \n- [ ] 5.3 Topology on $\\mathbb{R}$ [[Derivative of a set]] [[Closure of a set]]\n\n## Week 6: Accumulation Points\n\n- [ ] 6.1  Frontier of a set. Accumulation points on the reals.\n- [ ] 6.2 [[Compactness Set Real]]  **Here we end with Compact Sets**. [[Lateral Accumulation Points On The Reals]].\n- [ ] 6.3 Functions ,Limit composition, [[Limits (One Dimension)]]\n\n## Week 7: Limits of real functions\n- [ ] 7.1 [[Adherent Point of a real function]]. limit theorems\n- [ ] 7.2 Infinite Limits, [[Lateral Limits]], [[Lateral Accumulation Points On The Reals]] [[Cantor Set]].\n- [ ] 7.3 Superior and inferior limit. [[superior and inferior limit functions]].\n\n## Week 9 . Continuous Functions (Oct 21 - 28)\n- [ ] 9.1 Continuous Functions, types of discontinuous. [[Continuity (One Dimension)]] Uniformly continuous.[[Uniformly Continuous Function]]\n- [ ] 9.2 Inter-medium Value Theorem\n- [ ] 9.3 Continuous Functions on Compact Setsa\n\n\n Minimum and maximum value on Compactness sets, [[Closure of a set]], [[Compactness Set Real]], [[Limits (One Dimension)]] Close Sets, [[Functions Irrationals]] \n\n## Week 10. Derivatives (Nov 3 - 10) \n\n- [ ] 10.1 Uniformly continuous function. Sequences for functions to prove the continuity.\n- [ ] 10.2 [[derivatives]], lateral derivatives.\n- [ ] 10.3 Theorems related to the derivative, Rolle Theorem, Intermedium value function for derivatives.\n### 10.1 Qualified Practice \n\nAbout cauchy sequences and functions. About compactnessm that stuff\n\n## Week 11. Integral (Nov 10 - 17)\n\n- [ ] 11.1\n- [ ] 11.2\n\n### 11. Guided Practice\n\n## Week 12. Taylor (Nov 17-24) \n\n- [ ] 12.1\n- [ ] 12.2\n\n### 12. Qualified Practice\n\nAbout\n\n## Week 13. Integral (Nov 24-31)\n\n- [ ] 13.1 \n- [ ] 13.1 Characterization of the integrable functions,\nSuccessions of real function function, Uniform convergence, \n\n### 13.1. Guided Practice\n\nProblems\n\n---\n## Week 14. Series (Dec 01 -07)\n\n- [ ] 14.1 \n- [ ] 14.2 \n\n### 14.1  Qualified Practice \n\n## Week 15: Integrals (Dec 07 - Dec 14)\n\n\n\n## Week 16. Final Exam (Dec 18)\n\nQuestion 1.\n\n\n",
