    "title": "Capacitor Plaques Paralels",
    "excerpt": "Approximate the plaques: So the [[Potential Difference]] $\\Delta V$ could be written as:",
    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-10-29 11:22\nmodified: 2025-10-29 11:44\n---\nApproximate the plaques: So the [[Potential Difference]] $\\Delta V$ could be written as:\n$$\\Delta V=E.d$$\nWhere $d$ is the distance between the plaques, now what form takes $E$?\n \n Using the [[Gauss Law]] (using a cylinder) you obtain: $$E=\\frac{\\sigma}{\\varepsilon_{o}}$$ Where $\\varepsilon_{0}$ is the [[Electrical Permittivity on the Vaccum]] and $\\sigma$ is the charge density over the plaques. Thus:\n \n  $$\\frac{Q}{\\Delta V}=\\frac{Q}{Ed}=\\frac{Q\\varepsilon}{\\frac{Q}{A}d}=\\frac{Q}{ \\frac{\\sigma}{\\varepsilon}d} \\\\\n  =\\frac{\\varepsilon A}{d}$$\n",
