    "title": "Quantum Chemistry Units",
    "excerpt": "[[Quantum Numbers]] also called **atomic units**. (a.u) Hartree atomic units",
    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-10-29 08:20\nmodified: 2025-11-01 15:05\n---\n[[Quantum Numbers]] also called **atomic units**. (a.u) Hartree atomic units\n\nNatural system \n\n**Distance**: So the Bohr radius is :\n$$ a_{0}=\\frac{4\\pi\\varepsilon_{0}\\hbar^{2}}{m_{e}e^{2}}\\approx 0.529 \\overset{\\circ}{\\text{A}} $$\nWhere $\\overset{\\circ}{\\text{A}}=10^{-10}$ is called **Armstrong**.\n\n**Energy**: Hartree energy $E_{h}$\n\n$$\nE_{h}=\\frac{e^{2}}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_{0}a_{0}}\n$$\n\n**Time**:\n\n$$\nt_{0}=\\frac{\\hbar}{E_{h}}\n$$\n\n**Velocity**:\n\n$$\nv_{0}=\\frac{a_{0}}{t_{0}} \\approx 2.19\\times 10^{6}m /s\n$$\n\nI think that example would be amazing!.",
