    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-10-22 10:26\nmodified: 2025-10-22 10:42\n---\nA ordered field is when you first establish a [[Binary Relation]] and that order relation follow the condition: [^1]\n- The **relation** is total, just one of this is true: \n- The **relation** is compatible with the operations $+,\\times$ of the [[Field]].\n\nNow we can talk about the **Arquimidiean property**.\n\n$$\n\\forall x\\in \\mathbb{F},\\exists n\\in \\mathbb{N}|n>x\n$$\n\nIf you flip it:\n\n$$\n\\forall x\\in \\mathbb{F},\\exists n\\in \\mathbb{N}|\\frac{1}{n}<x\n$$\n\n[^1]: [[Analisis Real Elon Lages]] pp. 27\n",
