    "title": "Schrodinger Equation Many Bodies",
    "excerpt": "After understand the [[One electron Schrodinger Equation]], using one dimension, two dimension and three dimension",
    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: 2025-10-14 08:08\nmodified: 2026-01-24 10:53\n---\nAfter understand the [[One electron Schrodinger Equation]], using one dimension, two dimension and three dimension\n\nHere the [[Hamiltonian Operator]] operator becomes hard: [[Hamiltonian Operator for Molecules]]. Two flavors:\nUsing the [[Density Functional Theory]], which not solve the equation but finds another part to extract physical information or if you want to use [[Neural Wave Functions]]:\nInteresting approaches that I want to dive in: (In order of complexity)\n- Slater - Jastrow Ansatz\n- Fermi Net\n- Pauli Net\n- Psi Former\n- \n\n\n[^1]: [[Quantum Mechanics Zettili]] pp. 472",
    "uploadDate": "2025-10-14 08:08",
