    "id": "327",
    "title": "The Curse Of Dimensionalization FDM",
    "excerpt": "On the $X$ dimension, you have to generate a grid, but what about the $Y$ dimension you have to also do it, for $N=50$ you have to calculate $N^{2}$, ...",
    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\ndate: \"2025-10-11 21:44\"\nmodified: 2025-08-06T23:12:25-05:00\n---\nOn the $X$ dimension, you have to generate a grid, but what about the $Y$ dimension you have to also do it, for $N=50$ you have to calculate $N^{2}$, for $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$ $50^{3}$, it grows exponentially, so the options are [[Monthe Carlo Method]].\n\nBut we have to ask why this doesn't happen to [[PINNS]]. (They are computationally expensive in their way)\n\nI create a grid on a , it's not the same?\n\n[[Curse of Dimensionality]]",
