    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\nauthor: Jorge\ndate: 2025-09-28 20:30\nmodified: 2025-12-22 09:58\n---\nSo this is the one that professor recommends me:\n\nIn each point is:\n$$ E_{i}=\\frac{\\lvert y_{i}-\\hat{y}_{i} \\rvert }{\\lvert {y}_{i} \\rvert} $$\n- This means that the error becomes zero when there exist a perfect match.\n- The question is if it's bounded. Not necessarily.\n- Pretty good because it's not pretty close to zero all the time.\n\nNobody use it like a [[Loss Function on Neural Networks]], is more a [[Error metric]]\n",
