    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\nauthor: Jorge\ndate: 2025-09-19 13:26\nmodified: 2025-09-19 13:48\n---\nI am going to make something which is not normal, take the partial derivatives to [[Neural Network]]. But you don't want the partial derivative at a specific point. Sense.\n\n\nSo they have a list of functions that they know they derivatives and by making a **forward** you can compute the backward.\n\nI mean is basically [[Back propagation algorithm]] but the question is how they do it with non nice formulas.\n\nBut for the most of the cases is pretty well. Toy example! You have one input and two neurons and one output, how you take the derivative over the input? Of course at one specific point how you calculate the derivative of that point?\n\n[[graphs and autodif pytorch]]",
