    "id": "377",
    "title": "Dirichlet Condition Heat Equation One Dimension",
    "excerpt": "Using the Dirichlet Condition: $u(0,t)=0\\land u(L,t)=0$",
    "content": "---\ntags:\n  - baby\nauthor: Jorge\ndate: 2025-09-18 17:21\nmodified: 2025-09-18 17:34\n---\n\nUsing the Dirichlet Condition: $u(0,t)=0\\land u(L,t)=0$\n$$\nu(x,t)=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}b_{n}\\sin\\left( \\frac{n\\pi}{L}x \\right)e^{ -\\alpha(n\\pi/L^{2})t }\n$$\n$$ b_{n}=\\frac{2}{L}\\int_{0}^{L}f(x)\\sin\\left( \\frac{n\\pi x}{L} \\right)dx $$\n\nWith:\n$$f(x)=1-(x-1)^{2}$$\n$$L=2$$\nWith $\\alpha$ arbitrary.\n",
